<title>HUNGARY: Inter-Europa Bank cuts prime rate to 26pct.</title>
<headline>Inter-Europa Bank cuts prime rate to 26pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Inter-Europa Bank said on Tuesday that it will reduce its prime lending rates on forint loans to 26 percent from the current 26.875 percent.</p>
<p>The reduction will take effect on September 6.</p>
<p>Inter-Europa Bank is a member of Italy's San Paolo banking group.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
